{
  "engine": "front-end-with-html",
  "graderHint": "computeAllScores",
  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the four-instrument PRO battery (SF-36 RAND-method domains + non-licensed pcsApprox/mcsApprox, NDI, mJOA, EQ-5D-3L with the Dolan 1997 UK TTO value set). computeAllScores (composite.js) is the true entry point and simply aggregates the four independent instrument scorers; there is no cross-instrument composite, no bands beyond NDI/mJOA, and no flags. Every SF-36 item is linearly recoded to 0-100 on its own scale/polarity and each domain is the unweighted mean of its ANSWERED items (unanswered items are dropped from the mean, not scored as zero); pcsApprox = mean(pf, rp, bp, gh) and mcsApprox = mean(vt, sf, re, mh) over the non-null domains. healthChangeVsYearAgo is collected but unscored. NDI: percentageScore = rawScore / (5 x answeredSections) x 100, so a skipped section (e.g. driving for a non-driver) rescales the denominator; bands <5 no-disability, <15 mild, <25 moderate, <35 severe, else complete. mJOA needs all six items or returns null/''; bands >=15 mild, >=12 moderate, else severe. EQ-5D needs all five dimensions; '11111' is exactly 1.0, otherwise 1 - 0.081 - sum(level-2/3 dimension coefficients) - 0.269 if any dimension is level 3 (the N3 term); the index can be negative (33333 = -0.594, worse than dead). Floating-point values in 'expected' are whatever JavaScript produces (e.g. 83.33333333333333, 0.6910000000000001) - do not round them by hand; regenerate with: bin/test-personas patient-reported-outcome-measures --update",
